Sometimes 2 customers come and want to buy the same shoe, but one gets the price of $60 and the other $80? Why is that?

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Ask the interviewer that do we have different discounts for different customer as well. That can be one probable reason.
- Or there can be price or discount update when second customer is trying to buy the shoe.
- Or is there no any difference between color, size, brand or modelName. If there is no any difference then there can be multiple entries for this combination which is really a bad thing and we can have a unique constraint over this combination in the DB table.

